Based on my search, here's what I found regarding the Biome issue #1794 and the related fix:

## Issue #1794: Override globals are ignored

The original bug was reported for Biome version 1.5.3. The issue "🐛 Override globals are ignored" (#1794) was opened by anonrig on February 12, 2024. The problem occurred with a configuration like this:

```json
{
  "linter": {
    "enabled": true,
    "rules": {
      "all": true,
      "suspicious": { "noConsoleLog": "off" }
    }
  },
  "overrides": [
    {
      "include": ["hello/test"],
      "javascript": { "globals": ["test", "expect"] }
    }
  ]
}
```

In this scenario, the `globals` defined in the `overrides` section (such as `test` and `expect`) were being ignored rather than applied when linting the matching files.

## Related context on overrides inheritance

A more recent related fix addresses how override settings interact with global configuration. Formatter, linter, and assist settings now correctly inherit from global configuration when not explicitly specified in overrides. Before this fix, when an override specified only one feature (e.g., only linter), other features would be incorrectly disabled instead of inheriting from global settings. After this fix, .vue files will have the linter disabled (as specified in the override) but the formatter enabled (inherited from global settings).

