+      "body": "> As the CONTRIBUTING.md says, I used Claude Code to generate an implementation plan. It helped me write part of the implementation code, some of which was hallucinated and the rest I had to fix myself many times. Finally, it ported for me all test examples from the original [https://github.com/keithamus/sort-package-json](https://github.com/keithamus/sort-package-json) test suite.\r\n\r\nI opened this PR after https://github.com/biomejs/biome/discussions/941#discussioncomment-7715731.\r\n\r\nFirst of all, I haven’t written Rust since [2023](https://github.com/arthurfiorette/brainease), so my code is probably not optimal or may not use recent features. Feel free to bash me.\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nAn assist action, `organizePackageJson`, is being introduced (with a safe fix) to reorder a user’s package.json based on the infamous [https://www.npmjs.com/package/sort-package-json](https://www.npmjs.com/package/sort-package-json) package.\r\n\r\n**This PR heavily relies on the upstream JS implementation, in some places it is exactly the same code. The implementation was fairly easy, as it was mostly a translation from JS to Rust.**\r\n\r\nBefore reviewing, I recommend reading [sort-package-json/defaultRules.md](https://github.com/keithamus/sort-package-json/blob/main/defaultRules.md) and possibly [sort-package-json/index.js](https://github.com/keithamus/sort-package-json/blob/main/index.js) to understand how the sorting is done.\r\n\r\nAll the sorting logic implemented here has a corresponding implementation in JS provided by sort-package-json. This means that Biome should be able to produce matching output to the aforementioned package. No new features were added, this PR only mimics the package’s behavior.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhile implementing this, I noticed that `crates/biome_json_syntax/src/generated.rs` was not referencing the generated `nodes_mut` file, unlike other `generated.rs` files in other crates, and I needed `JsonArrayValue::with_elements`. After adding it myself, I had to remove some duplicated references in `crates/biome_json_syntax/src/member_ext.rs` and `crates/biome_json_syntax/src/object_ext.rs`, but I am not sure if that is the correct approach, a dedicated review there is needed.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\nBesides some inline tests and two basic tests, the entire test suite from [https://github.com/keithamus/sort-package-json](https://github.com/keithamus/sort-package-json) was rewritten here to ensure it is working correctly. I assume we can expect 1:1 behavior.\r\n\r\nIn the future, we could create a set of test files and run them against both Biome and `sort-package-json` to ensure they produce the same output.\r\n\r\n## Docs\r\n\r\nDocumentation is included inline via rustdoc, with before/after examples and references to the authoritative [sort-package-json defaultRules](https://github.com/keithamus/sort-package-json/blob/main/defaultRules.md).\r\n",
